e7 wire log v1
device   GS Music e7, serial 361, USB, driven from Node over CoreMIDI
input    GS-e7 Analog Synthesizer
output   GS-e7 Analog Synthesizer
date     2026-08-19
session  A session opened while an earlier one's answer was still pending, which is how a single Read Memory comes to draw two frames without the device sending two

# The shape protocol-quirks.md #12 called a preview frame, manufactured entirely
# host-side. A previous session sent a Read Memory and closed before its answer
# shipped; this session opened without draining and its first command flushed the
# tail of that answer as a frame of its own. What follows is one short frame no
# decoder accepts, then the real spec-shaped response behind it.
#
# The instrument sent no prelude in either session. Web MIDI never shows this
# because it delivers a whole F0..F7 frame per event; a native CoreMIDI client
# sees the pieces.
    +0.0ms  -->  F0 00 21 62 01 10 0E 00 00 00 F7
    +8.1ms  <--  F7
  +901.4ms  -->  F0 00 21 62 01 10 0E 00 00 00 F7
  +909.2ms  <--  F0 00 05 05 07 0D 06 00 07 09 06 0E 06 00 02 00 05 01 06 04 06 00 02 00 02 00 02 00 02 00 02 00 02 F7
